  "worked_solution": "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt[3]{x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt[3]{y} \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{y} & =-\\frac{3}{2}x \\\\ (\\sqrt[3]{y})^{3} & ={(-\\frac{3}{2}x)}^{3} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{27}{8}{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=-\\frac{27}{8}{x}^{3}.\n$$",
